      "description": "Build the three-storey single-bay frame from the attachment. Keep D, W+ and W- as independent signed cases, and evaluate the three explicitly listed combinations D, D+W+ and D+W-. D includes an additional downward 5 kN/m on the left half of the second-storey beam, in addition to its baseline 10 kN/m. Distinguish case D from combination D in labels. Report global Ux and Uz at the highest-storey rightmost beam-column joint, and global support My and Rz (=Fz) at the leftmost ground-level column base for every original load case and every listed combination, with signs and units.\nUse the stated OpenSees engine for every computable changed state. First-order linear elastic analysis; self-weight, P-delta, rigid diaphragms, rigid offsets and construction stages are off. Preserve all fields not explicitly changed. Report every requested signed value with node/member, global direction, unit, case/combination, turn, model state and traceable run ID. Rz denotes the vertical support reaction Fz. Retain original cases and evaluate every listed combination separately. Resolve essential missing or contradictory inputs before reporting new numerical results.",
